{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK6bt5itHvnDsW5ffG71","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`HttpResponse(memoryview(b\"My Content\")).content` now returns `b'My Content'`, as the issue expects. The `httpwrappers` and `responses` test modules pass.\n\nThe fix is two small changes in `django/http/response.py`:\n- **`make_bytes`:** it now converts a `memoryview` straight to bytes, the same way it already handled `bytes`. Before, it fell through to `str(value)`, which produced `b'<memory at 0x...>'`.\n- **The `content` setter:** a `memoryview` has `__iter__`, so the setter was treating it like a list of chunks and joining them one by one. It's now passed through as a single value, like `bytes` and `str` are."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":773,"cache_read_input_tokens":19285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":773},"output_tokens":231,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43554b9a-2393-4c33-823a-2a2ff12630ea","uuid":"86ceb78b-ccdb-40e6-9d21-036bebce1ee6","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:48:32.804Z","request_id":"req_011ChK6bsxHEHtBNvSJUqwfu"}
